## 3. The Klein Orbit Theorem

This section proves that the Klein group acts on the fourteen-mode multiplet with five size-two orbits and one size-four orbit.

### 3.1 Orbit decomposition

**Theorem (Klein Orbit Theorem).** The Klein four-group generated by the diagonal reflection and the half-period translation acts on the fourteen-mode multiplet with orbit decomposition consisting of five orbits of size two and one orbit of size four. Explicitly, the orbits are:

| Orbit | Members | Size |
|---|---|---|
| V-one | neutrino, electron | 2 |
| V-two | Higgs, Z boson | 2 |
| V-three | down quark, bottom quark | 2 |
| V-four | muon, charm quark | 2 |
| V-five | W boson, top quark | 2 |
| V-six | dark photon, strange quark, up quark, tau | 4 |

The total mode count is five times two plus one times four, which equals fourteen, matching the multiplicity at the self-paired eigenvalue.

**Proof.** Direct computation of the orbit of each mode under the Klein group. We compute representative orbits.

**Orbit of the neutrino at (zero, four).** The identity fixes the neutrino. The diagonal reflection sends it to the electron at (four, zero). The half-period translation sends it to the electron at (four, zero). The product sends it back to the neutrino at (zero, four). The orbit is the pair consisting of the neutrino and the electron, size two. This is V-one.

**Orbit of the Higgs at (six, two).** The identity fixes the Higgs. The diagonal reflection sends it to the Z boson at (two, six). The half-period translation sends it to the Z boson at (two, six). The product sends it back to the Higgs at (six, two). The orbit is the pair consisting of the Higgs and the Z boson, size two. This is V-two.

**Orbit of the down quark at (one, five).** The identity fixes the down quark. The diagonal reflection sends it to the bottom quark at (five, one). The half-period translation sends it to the bottom quark at (five, one). The product sends it back to the down quark at (one, five). The orbit is the pair consisting of the down quark and the bottom quark, size two. This is V-three.

**Orbit of the muon at (three, seven).** The identity fixes the muon. The diagonal reflection sends it to the charm quark at (seven, three). The half-period translation sends it to the charm quark at (seven, three). The product sends it back to the muon at (three, seven). The orbit is the pair consisting of the muon and the charm quark, size two. This is V-four.

**Orbit of the W boson at (two, two).** The identity fixes the W boson. The diagonal reflection also fixes the W boson, because it is a fixed point of the reflection. The half-period translation sends it to the top quark at (six, six). The product sends it to the top quark at (six, six). The orbit is the pair consisting of the W boson and the top quark, size two. This is V-five.

**Orbit of the dark photon at (five, seven).** The identity fixes the dark photon. The diagonal reflection sends it to the tau at (seven, five). The half-period translation sends it to the up quark at (one, three). The product sends it to the strange quark at (three, one). The orbit is the four-element set consisting of the dark photon, the tau, the up quark, and the strange quark, size four. This is V-six.

The six orbits cover all fourteen modes. The orbit decomposition is as in the statement.

### 3.2 The three structural regions

The orbit decomposition partitions the fourteen-mode multiplet into three structural regions.

**The four two-cycle orbits V-one through V-four.** Each of these orbits has two members that are exchanged by the diagonal reflection and by the half-period translation, and that are fixed by the product of the two generators. They are the framework's standard mirror pairs.

**The observer orbit V-five.** This orbit is the pair consisting of the W boson and the top quark, the observer pair of HCSM-26. Both members are fixed by the diagonal reflection.

**The four-cycle orbit V-six.** This orbit contains four modes that are cyclically exchanged by the Klein group. It contains the swap partner of the top quark — see Section 5 — and has the framework-constant property of Section 6.

**Remark.** The four-cycle orbit V-six contains the modes up quark, strange quark, dark photon, and tau, all drawn from the middle dihedral orbit of size eight. The Klein group therefore further refines the middle dihedral orbit: the dihedral orbit of size eight splits into the three Klein orbits V-three (down quark and bottom quark), V-four (muon and charm quark), and V-six (dark photon, strange quark, up quark, and tau).

