## 7. Discussion

### 7.1 What the Klein structure gives

The Klein four-group generated by the diagonal reflection and the half-period translation organizes the fourteen-mode multiplet into six orbits:

- Four two-cycle orbits with pointwise stabilizer generated by the product of the two generators: V-one (neutrino and electron), V-two (Higgs and Z boson), V-three (down quark and bottom quark), V-four (muon and charm quark).
- One two-cycle orbit with pointwise stabilizer generated by the diagonal reflection: the observer orbit V-five (W boson and top quark).
- One four-cycle orbit with trivial pointwise stabilizer: V-six (dark photon, strange quark, up quark, tau).

The orbit-class swap pair is the unique bridge between the four-cycle orbit and the observer orbit. This is the framework's minimal connective structure between its two most distinctive orbits.

### 7.2 Refinement of the dihedral orbit partition

The dihedral orbit partition of the fourteen-mode multiplet is:

- Orbit zero: neutrino, electron.
- Orbit one: up quark, down quark, strange quark, muon, dark photon, charm quark, tau, bottom quark.
- Orbit two: W boson, Z boson, Higgs, top quark.

The Klein orbit partition refines the dihedral orbit partition:

- Orbit zero is the single Klein orbit V-one.
- Orbit one decomposes into three Klein orbits: V-three, V-four, and V-six.
- Orbit two decomposes into two Klein orbits: V-two and V-five.

The Klein group therefore provides a fine-grained partition of the multiplet, in which each dihedral orbit of size greater than two is further decomposed.

### 7.3 Relation to the observer pair

The observer pair of HCSM-26 is the Klein orbit V-five. Its pointwise stabilizer is generated by the chiral reflection. This is consistent with the Chirality Selection Theorem: the observer pair is the unique fixed locus of the chiral reflection on the fourteen-mode multiplet.

The four-cycle orbit V-six has trivial pointwise stabilizer. Its swap partner with the observer orbit is the top quark, which lies in V-five. The two most distinctive orbits of the Klein structure are connected by the swap pair consisting of the dark photon and the top quark.

