## 9. Conclusion

This paper has characterized the Klein orbit structure of the fourteen-mode multiplet in the Hodge Complex Standard Model. The Klein four-group generated by the diagonal reflection and the half-period translation acts on the multiplet with orbit decomposition consisting of five two-cycle orbits and one four-cycle orbit. The pointwise stabilizer of each orbit is one of the three non-trivial subgroups of the Klein group: four orbits have stabilizer generated by the product of the two generators, the observer orbit has stabilizer generated by the diagonal reflection, and the four-cycle orbit has trivial stabilizer. The four-cycle orbit contains the framework-constant shadow of the Hodge sector: its four mass-ordering labels are all framework constants, they satisfy two additive identities within the orbit, and their sum equals fifty-six, the dimension of the Hodge sector at the self-paired eigenvalue. Their mean equals fourteen, the multiplicity.

The orbit-class swap pair, consisting of the dark photon and the top quark, is the unique edge in the distinguished-pair graph that connects two distinct Klein orbits. It bridges the four-cycle orbit and the observer orbit, providing the framework's minimal connective structure between its two most distinctive orbits.

The Klein structure organizes the fourteen-mode multiplet in a way that refines the dihedral orbit partition and brings the framework-constant arithmetic of the four-cycle orbit into focus. The observer pair of HCSM-26 is the orbit V-five of this structure, and the framework-constant orbit is V-six.

